  "summary": "ShadowV2 is a DDoS-for-hire botnet whose Go-based ELF implant is deployed into exposed Docker daemons (observed against AWS EC2 honeypots) via a Python spreader running from GitHub CodeSpaces. The unstripped implant registers with a FastAPI/Pydantic C2 at shadow.aurozacloud[.]xyz, heartbeats every second, polls for commands every five seconds, and launches HTTP floods including HTTP/2 rapid reset and a ChromeDP-based Cloudflare UAM bypass. Detection should focus on the implant's Go symbol and string artifacts, the /app/deployment drop path, the Docker SDK user agent, and the C2 API endpoints.",
